  "name": "pairwise_pref_loss",
  "intuition": "This loss compares pairwise log probabilities to encourage the model to assign higher probabilities to preferred options. By using logsigmoid on the difference, it emphasizes relative ranking, making the model learn to prefer better options consistently. This approach directly encodes preference signals and leverages pairwise comparisons, leading to robust preference modeling.",
  "pseudocode": "loss = -mean(logsigmoid(log_prob_w - log_prob_l) * (cost_b - cost_a))",
